{%- comment -%}
  THE CAROUSEL — the rail, rebuilt as a circle.

  A rail is a straight line: you pull it sideways and the end arrives. This is
  the same idea bent into a ring — the garments stand around a circle, the one
  facing you is the front, and the ring turns. Two things turn it:

    · scrolling (the wheel on a desktop, a finger on a phone) — one notch per
      click, with a spring so it lands rather than stops dead;
    · dragging it with the pointer, which is the same gesture at a different
      speed.

  On a phone the whole panel is pinned while the collection is in this view, so
  the screen holds still and the clothes are what move. `--mf-ring-span` is the
  scroll distance reserved for a full turn; past it the page carries on.

  The maths. Each piece sits at `angle = (i - active) × step`, and the ring's
  own rotation is `-active × step`. A piece therefore arrives at 0° — facing the
  viewer, nearest the eye — exactly when it becomes the active one, and the
  other pieces stand further back along the circle. `translateZ` is what makes
  the front one bigger; `perspective` on the stage is what makes that read as
  depth rather than as resizing.

  Parameters
    products  the array to hang (required)
    eyebrow   optional small line above the ring
    heading   optional heading; omit inside the collection view
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ring_garments = products | where: 'available', true -%}

<div class="mf-circle" data-rack data-circle>
  {%- if heading != blank or eyebrow != blank -%}
    <header class="mf-circle__head">
      {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="mf-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if heading != blank -%}<h2>{{ heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
    </header>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="mf-circle__stage" data-circle-stage>
    {%- comment -%} the ring the pieces stand on, drawn once and turned by JS {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="mf-circle__ring" data-circle-ring>
      <span class="mf-circle__post mf-circle__post--back" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="mf-circle__floor" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      {%- capture circle_items -%}
      {%- for product in ring_garments -%}
        {%- assign slot = product.metafields.molfet.slot.value | default: 'top' -%}
        {%- if slot == 'accessory' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign cutout = product.metafields.molfet.cutout -%}
        <li class="mf-circle__item" data-circle-item data-slot="{{ slot }}"
          style="--i: {{ forloop.index0 }};">
          <a class="mf-circle__link" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="mf-circle__figure">
              {%- if cutout != blank or product.featured_image != blank -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ cutout | default: product.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 }}"
                  alt="{{ product.title | escape }}"
                  width="320" height="420"
                  loading="lazy" draggable="false">
              {%- else -%}
                {% render 'media-placeholder', class: 'mf-circle__img', ratio: '3/4' %}
              {%- endif -%}
              <span class="mf-circle__shine" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {{- circle_items -}}

      {%- assign circle_check = circle_items | strip -%}
      {%- if circle_check == blank -%}
        <p class="mf-circle__empty">{{ 'rack.empty' | t }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The front piece, in words. It is a real link, it is what a screen reader
    reads, and it is the only thing that can be tapped when the ring is behind
    it — which is why the individual figures are hidden from the focus order.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="mf-circle__hud">
    <p class="mf-circle__count" aria-live="polite">
      <span data-circle-index>1</span><span class="mf-circle__slash">/</span><span data-circle-total>{{ ring_garments.size }}</span>
    </p>
    <a class="mf-circle__title" href="#" data-circle-front>{{ 'rack.title' | t }}</a>
    <p class="mf-circle__price" data-circle-price></p>
  </div>

  <div class="mf-circle__controls">
    <button type="button" class="mf-circle__step" data-circle-prev
      aria-label="{{ 'rack.previous' | t }}">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="16" height="16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M12 4l-6 6 6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
    </button>

    <span class="mf-circle__dots" data-circle-dots aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <button type="button" class="mf-circle__step" data-circle-next
      aria-label="{{ 'rack.next' | t }}">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="16" height="16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M8 4l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
    </button>
  </div>

  {%- unless request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="mf-circle__span" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {%- endunless -%}
</div>
